State return (Illinois)
- Illinois uses IL‑1040. Illinois generally starts with federal AGI as a starting point and then applies state modifications. Interest income is generally taxable at the Illinois flat rate (check current rate; historically ~4.95%). Illinois has limited itemized deduction options; in most cases you’ll use the federal AGI plus state adjustments. Check Illinois Department of Revenue guidance or ask a tax pro for state specifics.

