2. Use the actual home‑office method (Form 8829) because the rent portion gives a much larger deduction than the simplified method in your numbers.
3. Report web‑design income on Schedule C and claim business expenses there (including the home office). That will lower your AGI and self‑employment tax.
4. Claim student loan interest on Schedule 1 up to $2,500 if the interest was paid in 2024 and your MAGI is within limits.
5. Likely take the standard deduction on Form 1040 unless you have substantial additional itemizable deductions.
6. Keep all receipts and 1098‑E (student loan interest statement), 1099s, donation receipts, and documents supporting home office size and rent/utilities.
7. Consider using tax software or a CPA — the home‑office, QBI, and student loan phaseout nuances are easy to get right with professional review.

