- W‑2 income: reported on Form 1040; nothing special to deduct here except payroll withholding and any pre-tax benefits shown on the W‑2.
- Self‑employment income (web design): report on Schedule C. You can deduct ordinary and necessary business expenses on Schedule C (software, hosting, client expenses, supplies, phone portion, etc.). If any portion of your $890 “unreimbursed expenses” relates to this self‑employment work, include them on Schedule C. If they are employee unreimbursed expenses (as an employee of Riverside Hospital), those are not deductible on the federal return for tax years 2018–2025 (suspended by the TCJA).
