- The home‑office deduction (for self‑employed taxpayers) cannot exceed net profit from that business. That is, you cannot create or increase a Schedule C loss by applying the business’s deductible home‑office portion — excess home‑office deduction may be suspended and carried forward to future years (there are specific rules).
