Key things you can (likely) deduct
- Self‑employment business expenses: The $890 — if those are business expenses for your web design work (supplies, software, hosting, mileage, etc.), they are deductible on Schedule C and reduce your net self‑employment income. If those are unreimbursed employee expenses for an employer job, they are NOT deductible for federal returns (suspended under current law).
- Home office: You can take a home‑office deduction for your self‑employment web design if the office is used regularly and exclusively for the business. You can choose either:
