Thanks — I can walk through how each item is treated, give a rough computation, and list the forms you’ll likely need. A couple of quick clarifying questions before I finalize numbers:
- Were the student-loan interest payments actually paid in tax year 2024 (and do you have a 2024 Form 1098‑E from Navient)? You mentioned 2016–2019, which would not be deductible on a 2024 return.
- Are the $890 “unreimbursed expenses” employee expenses tied to a W‑2 job, or are they business expenses related to your web‑design work? (That changes whether and how they’re deductible.)
