Thanks — I can walk through what’s deductible, how the home-office works, whether itemizing will likely help, and which federal/state forms you’ll need. A few quick clarifying questions first (they affect the answers):

- Did you actually pay $4,400 in student-loan interest during tax year 2024, or is that interest that was paid in 2016–2019 (i.e., earlier years)? The student-loan interest deduction only covers interest you paid during the tax year being filed.
