- Gather documents: W-2, any 1099-NEC/1099-MISC, 1099-INT, 1099-DIV/1099-B, rent receipts (12 months), charity receipt, records of business expenses.
- Decide home-office method. Given your numbers, regular method with Form 8829 typically gives a larger deduction.
- Use tax software or consult a CPA/tax preparer to:
  - Properly compute Schedule C, Form 8829, Schedule SE, and any QBI deduction.
  - Confirm student loan interest eligibility and income-phaseout rules.
  - Prepare federal Form 1040 and Illinois Form IL-1040.

If you want, I can:
