  - Net SE income ≈ $8,900 − $5,088 = $3,812
  - Net earnings for SE tax = ~92.35% of net SE income ≈ $3,520
  - SE tax ≈ 15.3% × $3,520 ≈ $539 (approx.)
  - You can deduct half of SE tax (~$270) as an adjustment to income on Schedule 1 (reduces AGI).
- SE tax is calculated on Schedule SE; business profit is on Schedule C.

