- The student loan interest deduction is an above‑the‑line adjustment (reduces AGI) — very helpful.
- The maximum deduction allowed per return is $2,500 for the year (you cannot deduct the full $4,400 you paid). So you’ll be able to deduct up to $2,500, assuming you meet the income/filing status rules.
