  - Records/receipts for home office-related costs, utilities, and any business expenses (the $890), and copies of rent statements

8) Estimated taxes and withholding
- Because you have self‑employment income, you may owe additional income tax and self‑employment tax beyond what your W‑2 withholding covers. If you expect to owe more than $1,000 when you file, you should consider making quarterly estimated payments (Form 1040‑ES) to avoid penalties.

