- Decide home office method: actual method likely gives a bigger deduction for you; prepare the calculations and receipts (rent, utilities, insurance) — Form 8829 or equivalent documentation will be needed for actual method calculations.
- Prepare Schedule C and Schedule SE (or consult a tax preparer/tax software). Consider the QBI deduction (Form 8995).
- If you expect to owe additional tax this year because of self‑employment income, consider making estimated payments or adjusting withholding.

