- Schedule C (Profit or Loss from Business) — report web design income and business expenses, and claim home office deduction (or attach Form 8829 if using actual method)
- Schedule SE (Self‑Employment Tax) — computes SE tax and the half‑SE deduction
- Form 8829 (if you use the actual method and are calculating business use of home expenses; if you use the simplified method, you don’t use 8829)
- Form 8995 or 8995‑A (QBI deduction) — if applicable
- Schedule A (Itemized Deductions) — only if you choose to itemize (charitable donations, SALT up to cap, etc.)
- Schedule B (Interest and Ordinary Dividends) — only required if certain thresholds apply or you have certain foreign accounts; with your interest + dividends ($1,085) you are under typical Schedule B thresholds, but still report the amounts on Form 1040.
