6) Unreimbursed employee expenses
- Since 2018, miscellaneous unreimbursed employee expenses (suspension by TCJA) are not deductible on federal returns for most employees. If the $890 are employee unreimbursed expenses, those are not deductible federally (state rules may differ).
- If those $890 are business expenses for your self‑employment work, include them on Schedule C instead (they then reduce SE tax and income tax).

7) Itemize vs standard deduction
