- If you itemize, deductible as an itemized deduction (cash to qualified charitable organization). Keep your receipt. If you take the standard deduction you generally can't deduct it (unless special rules apply — e.g., certain limited-year universal charitable deductions, but those are temporary and specific).
- For a married couple filing jointly, you only itemize if total itemized deductions exceed the standard deduction.

7. Unreimbursed expenses ($890)
- If these are unreimbursed employee business expenses (for an employer W-2 job), miscellaneous unreimbursed employee expenses are not deductible through 2025 due to tax law changes.  
- If these are ordinary and necessary expenses of your web-design business (e.g., software licenses, client-related travel, materials) they belong on Schedule C as business expenses and are deductible against that self-employment income.

