- Based on the items you listed, the only clear itemized deduction is $2,000 in charitable contributions. You did not list mortgage interest, property taxes, or large medical expenses. Unless you have additional itemizable amounts (mortgage interest, significant state + local taxes up to the $10,000 SALT cap, large unreimbursed medical expenses exceeding 7.5% of AGI, or other deductible expenses), it is very likely the standard deduction will be larger than your total itemized deductions.  
