- Schedule 1 (Additional Income and Adjustments) — for reporting adjustments like student loan interest and the deductible half of self-employment tax.  
- Schedule C (Profit or Loss from Business) — to report your web-design income and business expenses.  
- Schedule SE (Self-Employment Tax) — to calculate SE tax.  
- Form 8829 (Expenses for Business Use of Your Home) — to compute the home-office deduction if you use the actual method. If you use the simplified method, you’ll calculate it on Schedule C directly.  
- Form 8995 (or 8995-A) — Qualified Business Income (QBI) deduction (20% of qualified business income) may apply for some self-employment income; with your numbers QBI effect will be small but check it when preparing Schedule C.  
- 1099-INTs / 1099-DIV / 1099-B statements (for interest/dividends/brokerage items).  
- Form 1098-E (student loan interest statement) — for interest paid in the tax year.  
- Illinois state return (IL-1040) — to file your state tax return. Illinois taxes interest and wages; check state rules for deductions/credits.  
- If you received any 1099-NEC for your client work, keep those for your records (they don’t change your filing requirement).

